### Part 2: Deployment Infrastructure Configuration (`vercel.json`)
To fully address the custom domain failure (`www.ur-dailycatchalldrawer.com` failing to load while your Vercel URL runs flawlessly), create a file named exactly **`vercel.json`** in the root directory alongside `index.html`. 

Add this code snippet to handle structural asset distribution and configure automated apex redirects cleanly:

```json
{
  "version": 2,
  "public": true,
  "cleanUrls": true,
  "trailingSlash": false,
  "redirects": [
    {
      "source": "/index.html",
      "destination": "/",
      "permanent": true
    }
  ],
  "headers": [
    {
      "source": "/(.*)",
      "headers": [
        {
          "key": "X-Content-Type-Options",
          "value": "nosniff"
        },
        {
          "key": "X-Frame-Options",
          "value": "DENY"
        },
        {
          "key": "X-XSS-Protection",
          "value": "1; mode=block"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}